# Execution records written by the robot client (not part of this release):
# per-run robot logs
# (actual joint_position/velocity/torque, wrist F/T, gripper widths, camera
# frames) -- tens of MB of diagnostics for a single run, not source. Keep the
# folder in git, ignore the records themselves.
*
!.gitignore
!.gitkeep

# The exception is a COMPLETE sweep of the grid, in a dated folder. Same argument
# plans/.gitignore makes for the event log -- for anything quoted as an execution
# result, the records ARE the result -- with one difference that makes it stronger:
# a plan can be replanned and a timing log re-measured, but a hardware run cannot
# be regenerated. The robot was in that state once. What is deliberately still
# ignored is the per-run debugging pickle: a single point re-executed while chasing
# a fault, and anything carrying camera frames (rgb_im/dep_im), which is where the
# tens of megabytes actually live.
#
# 2026-08-11: 20/20 points executed clean, 18.0 min, mean 54.1 s per point.
# See the folder README for the full record.
!2026-08-11/
!2026-08-11/*.pkl
